From: Banana <bananalinux@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 15:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] command: TOGGLE_ANALOG_DPAD, for a handheld with no analogue stick

The Retroid Pocket Classic is a stickless slate -- a d-pad, four face buttons
and the shoulders, no analogue stick. RetroArch's "Analog to Digital" (the
per-port input_analog_dpad_mode) is what makes a game that reads only the
analogue stick playable: the d-pad drives the emulated left stick. But there is
no hotkey and no command for it, only the Quick Menu's Controls page, which is
not reachable from inside every game.

This adds a command to the stdin/network interface banana already drives
(bananad writes /run/banana/retroarch.cmd): TOGGLE_ANALOG_DPAD toggles player 1
between the d-pad and "the d-pad drives the analogue stick", and says which on
screen. bananad sends it on F + B while a game runs.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [a specific handheld's controls]
---
--- a/command.h
+++ b/command.h
@@ -426,6 +426,7 @@
 bool command_get_status(command_t *cmd, const char* arg);
 bool command_get_config_param(command_t *cmd, const char* arg);
 bool command_show_osd_msg(command_t *cmd, const char* arg);
+bool command_toggle_analog_dpad(command_t *cmd, const char* arg);
 bool command_load_state_slot(command_t *cmd, const char* arg);
 bool command_play_replay_slot(command_t *cmd, const char* arg);
 bool command_seek_replay(command_t *cmd, const char *arg);
@@ -466,6 +467,7 @@
 
    { "LOAD_CORE", command_load_core, "<core path>"},
    { "AUDIO_REINIT", command_audio_reinit, "No argument"},
+   { "TOGGLE_ANALOG_DPAD", command_toggle_analog_dpad, "No argument"},
 };
 
 static const struct cmd_map map[] = {
--- a/command.c
+++ b/command.c
@@ -744,6 +744,30 @@
     return true;
 }
 
+
+
+/* The d-pad and the emulated left analogue stick: a handheld with no analogue stick (the Retroid Pocket Classic)
+ * can have RetroArch's "Analog to Digital" drive the stick from the d-pad, which is what a game that reads only the
+ * stick needs. banana's bananad sends this on F + B in a running game. */
+bool command_toggle_analog_dpad(command_t *cmd, const char* arg)
+{
+   settings_t *settings = config_get_ptr();
+   const char *msg      = NULL;
+
+   if (settings->uints.input_analog_dpad_mode[0] == ANALOG_DPAD_LSTICK)
+   {
+      settings->uints.input_analog_dpad_mode[0] = ANALOG_DPAD_NONE;
+      msg = "The d-pad is the d-pad";
+   }
+   else
+   {
+      settings->uints.input_analog_dpad_mode[0] = ANALOG_DPAD_LSTICK;
+      msg = "The d-pad is the analogue stick";
+   }
+   runloop_msg_queue_push(msg, strlen(msg), 1, 180, false, NULL,
+         MESSAGE_QUEUE_ICON_DEFAULT, MESSAGE_QUEUE_CATEGORY_INFO);
+   return true;
+}
 
 bool command_load_state_slot(command_t *cmd, const char *arg)
 {
